WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.131
Before you submit.

2
00:00:01.411 --> 00:00:07.085
Read the report summary aloud to someone outside engineering and ask them what they would decide.

3
00:00:07.365 --> 00:00:10.544
Check every number in the summary against the results table.

4
00:00:10.824 --> 00:00:17.843
Confirm the headline is held-out, with n and an interval, and that the number of held-out runs and variants is disclosed.

5
00:00:18.123 --> 00:00:24.608
Watch your demo once at normal speed as if you were a reviewer, and note the first moment you would have stopped trusting it.

6
00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:29.176
Confirm one command on a tagged commit reproduces the headline numbers.

7
00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:32.571
Then work through the defense checklist on the project page.

8
00:00:32.851 --> 00:00:40.851
When it is all green, you have something rarer than a working AI system: one whose quality, cost, and risks a stranger can verify.
